# Text files that tests embed byte for byte with `include_str`: their content and length must not
# depend on `core.autocrlf` (Windows checkouts would otherwise turn their line endings into CRLF).
tests/**/*.txt text eol=lf
# The sessions of the language server and their documents: positions in them count lines and
# columns, which must not depend on `core.autocrlf` either.
tests/lsp/* text eol=lf
# The corpus of each pass and the dumps expected from it (docs/adr/0066-test-harness-in-sagitario.md):
# the dumps hold byte offsets, which must be the same on every system. `crlf.sag` keeps `\r\n` line
# endings everywhere, for the lexer.
tests/lexer/** text eol=lf
tests/parser/** text eol=lf
tests/resolve/** text eol=lf
tests/types/** text eol=lf
tests/codegen/** text eol=lf
tests/lexer/crlf.sag text eol=crlf
# What the compiler embeds with `include_str` (the runtime, the prelude and the standard library)
# and the seed (docs/adr/0067-bootstrap-from-the-seed.md): the C the compiler generates must be the
# same on every system. The seed is generated: no diffs, and not counted as source by GitHub.
runtime/** text eol=lf
compiler/std/** text eol=lf
bootstrap/** text eol=lf
bootstrap/sag.c -diff linguist-generated
